<title>USA: Golden West Financial Corp Q3 net rises.</title>
<headline>Golden West Financial Corp Q3 net rises.</headline>
<text>
<p>OAKLAND, Calif., Oct 17 (Reuter)</p>
<p>			 Sept 30, 1996	     Sept 30, 1995</p>
<p> Shr primary     $	2.32	    $	1.08</p>
<p> Net		     135,785		  63,381</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary     57,584		  58,681</p>
<p>	  Nine months</p>
<p> Shr primary     $	1.52	    $	2.86</p>
<p> Net			 88,721		 167,875</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary     58,216		   58,637</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)  </p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 reflects one-time SAIF assessment of $132,587. In September 1996, Golden West Financial Corp. adopted SFAS 72 effective Jan. 1, 1996 for acquisitions prior to Sept. 30, 1982.  As a result, the company wrote off goodwill totalling $205,242 as the cumulative effect of the change in accounting for goodwill. The amounts for 1996 reflect a tax benefit of $139,485 arising from a prior year acquisition.</p>
</text>
